    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a balanced slate today, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who anchors the lineup with an elite score of 74.56. His prime spot batting second against the vulnerable arm of Holmes, G (4.71 xERA) provides the highest ceiling on the roster, bolstered by a significant 14% boost from his favorable dynamic platoon advantage. **Jacob Wilson** also projects as a top-tier play at 61.42; assuming he slides into the leadoff spot as expected, he benefits from a massive park-factor lift and the plate appearances necessary to chase stolen base production, our most critical scarcity. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** earns a strong 59.19 score, serving as a sneaky play today because the matchup against a high-ERA starter outweighs the inherent inefficiency of his nine-hole position.\n\nWhile **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** hover near the 60-point threshold, they are buoyed by favorable wind conditions at their venue, effectively canceling out the challenge posed by Bryan Woo\u2019s moderate 3.65 xERA. The most difficult bench decision involved balancing the volume of **Luis Robert Jr.** against his significant platoon-split penalty; despite his 47.30 score and the potential for a stolen base against the slow delivery of P\u00e9rez, Eu, his projected inefficiency kept him on the lower end of our starting confidence. We must remain cautious of the 32% rain risk looming over **Liam Hicks**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as any mid-game delay in their respective matchups could cap their production and hamper our daily efficiency goals. \n\nWith **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Cole Carrigg** unavailable due to scheduling or off-days, and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, our depth is thinner than usual. We are proceeding without the high-upside contributions of **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman**, placing the burden of performance squarely on **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas** to maximize their respective opportunities against Irvin, J and Weathers. Every stolen base attempt from our active roster is being monitored closely to navigate the volatility of today's matchups.",
